<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">26 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 26 June, from 684 to 1963.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/exarchate-of-ravenna" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/exarchate-of-ravenna.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">684 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,342 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Benedict II is consecrated pope after imperial approval</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Benedict II was consecrated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> after receiving the approval of the Byzantine emperor, as popes then required. He was the last pope to need the emperor's confirmation; his successors needed only that of the exarch of Ravenna.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/exarchate-of-ravenna">Exarchate of Ravenna</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1243">1243 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">783 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mongols crush the Seljuks of Rûm at Köse Dağ</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Mongol army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baiju">Baiju</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaykhusraw-ii">Kaykhusraw II</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. The Seljuk sultanate became a Mongol <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> and broke into the principalities from which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> emerged.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1295">1295 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">731 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Przemysł II is crowned King of Poland at Gniezno</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/przemysl-ii">Przemysł II</a>, Duke of Greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, was crowned King of Poland in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gniezno">Gniezno</a> Cathedral, the first royal coronation in Poland for over two centuries. He returned Poland to the rank of kingdom but was murdered at Rogoźno the following February.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/przemysl-ii">Przemysł II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1409">1409 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">617 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Council of Pisa elects Alexander V, a third rival pope</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Having declared Gregory XII of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and Benedict XIII of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avignon">Avignon</a> deposed, the Council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a> elected Peter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraklion">Candia</a> as Alexander V, a third claimant in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-schism">Western Schism</a>. He died in 1410 and is now regarded as an antipope.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-schism">Western Schism</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">Papacy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1460">1460 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">566 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Warwick and the Earl of March land at Sandwich</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Richard Neville, Earl of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warwick">Warwick</a>, landed at Sandwich with a rebel army and the Earls of Salisbury and March, and the three earls rode to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. Warwick and March went on to take King Henry captive at Northampton on 10 July.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-roses">Wars of the Roses</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iv-of-england">Edward IV of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1830">1830 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">196 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George IV dies at Windsor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The former Prince Regent, known for extravagance and his patronage of architecture, died at 67. His brother William IV succeeded him, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reform-act-1832">Great Reform Act</a> followed in 1832.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1857">1857 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">169 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Queen Victoria presents the first Victoria Crosses</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In Hyde Park, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/queen-victoria">Queen Victoria</a> decorated 62 servicemen for valour in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimean-war">Crimean War</a>. The Victoria Cross remains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s highest award for gallantry.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-kingdom-of-great-britain-and-ireland">United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimean-war">Crimean War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">United Nations Charter is signed in San Francisco</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates of 50 nations signed the Charter creating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> to maintain peace and security. It came into force in October 1945.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kennedy tells West Berlin 'Ich bin ein Berliner'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Speaking at Rathaus Schöneberg to a crowd of about 450,000, President Kennedy declared solidarity with the people of the walled city two years after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin-wall">Berlin Wall</a> went up.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 26 June <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/victor-amadeus-iii-of-sardinia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/victor-amadeus-iii-of-sardinia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Victor Amadeus III of Sardinia</span><span class="tp">1726–1796</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sunthorn-phu"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sunthorn-phu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sunthorn Phu</span><span class="tp">1786–1855</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bartolome-mitre"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bartolome-mitre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bartolomé Mitre</span><span class="tp">1821–1906</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/salvador-allende"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/salvador-allende.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Salvador Allende</span><span class="tp">1908–1973</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 26 June <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/giulio-alberoni"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/giulio-alberoni.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Giulio Alberoni</span><span class="tp">1664–1752</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/caesar-rodney"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/caesar-rodney.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Caesar Rodney</span><span class="tp">1728–1784</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-iv-of-the-united-kingdom"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-iv-of-the-united-kingdom.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George IV of the United Kingdom</span><span class="tp">1762–1830</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/kim-gu"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kim-gu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Kim Gu</span><span class="tp">1876–1949</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/algirdas-brazauskas"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/algirdas-brazauskas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Algirdas Brazauskas</span><span class="tp">1932–2010</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
